Z||000000||horseman||12-12-2000||07:26 PM||||HI All,<BR>I need to know if 235/60/14 tires will work on my stock 14" rims('84 se w/turbo fins). They are snow tires off of another car. I really need to find out if I will have any clearance problems or rim probs. It is supposed to snow 4-6" tommorrow.<BR>Thanks in advance,<BR>Charlie||||reg||5
Z||000001||terryk||12-12-2000||09:41 PM||||I've run them, but it's getting close on the sidewall angle. I would say it's about the limit.||||reg||1
Z||000002||RedOktober||12-12-2000||11:20 PM||||vlad is running that size here .. seems not to be having any problems.. But if they are snow tires.. they might be too wide... what you need is a set of 175/ 70 14's .. something to cut the snow and get to pavement...<BR>  ||||reg||1
Z||000003||N_Man||12-13-2000||01:39 AM||||redoktober hit it right on for snow tires the skinnier the better.<P>Ive got 185/70/14's and there great awsome traction.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Wannabe||12-13-2000||08:18 AM||||Just remember, if you live in the city, you won't be driving in the snow all the time.||||reg||1
Z||000005||horseman||12-13-2000||08:29 PM||||Cool guys,<BR>I realize now that they maybe a little wide for optimal snow traction, but they are free!<BR>I am just glad that they won't cause any interference and/or clearance problems.<BR>Charlie||||reg||14
